`CLASS_NAMES` is the module constant list of class names whose position is the class id: "wood", "grass", "wetland", "sand", "ice", "farmland", "rock", "residential", "pitch", "track", "cemetery", "hospital", "school", "university", "college", "kindergarten", "river", "canal", "stream", "ditch", "drain", "motorway", "trunk", "primary", "secondary", "tertiary", "minor", "service", "path", "rail", "transit", "raceway", "busway", "pier", "ferry", "runway" and "taxiway".

`class_id(name)` gives the position of the name in `CLASS_NAMES`, or -1 when it is not there.

`layer_id(name)` maps an OpenMapTiles layer name to its L_ constant ("water", "waterway", "landcover", "landuse", "park", "boundary", "aeroway", "transportation", "building", "water_name", "transportation_name", "place", "housenumber", "poi", "mountain_peak", "aerodrome_label"), or -1 for any other name.

`style_init()` fills the module list `rules` from `rows` once (it does nothing when `rules` is already filled). For each row: layer is `layer_id` of the row's layer; geom is GEOM_FILL for "fill", GEOM_LINE for "line" and GEOM_EDGE for "edge"; classes is a bit mask with bit `class_id` set for every space-separated name in the row's classes (the word "any" gives 0, meaning any class); brunnel is 0 for "any", 1 for "surface" and 2 for "bridge"; ramp is 0 for "any", 1 for "no" and 2 for "yes"; amin and amax are copied. Every number field is copied as it is.

`rule_matches(r, layer, gtype, a)` says whether a feature of that layer and geometry type with those attributes is drawn by rule r: the layer must equal; a GEOM_FILL or GEOM_EDGE rule takes only G_POLY features and a GEOM_LINE rule takes only G_LINE features; when classes is not 0 the feature's class id must be 0 or more and its bit must be set; brunnel 1 refuses features whose brunnel is 1 (a bridge) and brunnel 2 takes only features whose brunnel is 1; ramp 1 refuses ramps and ramp 2 takes only ramps; on the boundary layer the feature's admin level must be within amin and amax and maritime features are refused.

`feature_mask(layer, gtype, a)` is the 64 bit mask with bit i set for every rule i in `rules` that `rule_matches` the feature.

`rule_width(r, z)` is the line width in CSS pixels at zoom z from the three stops (za, wa), (zb, wb), (zc, wc): below za it is wa, above zc it is wc, and between two neighbouring stops it interpolates with base `base` the way MapLibre's exponential interpolation does: with d the stop gap and p the zoom past the lower stop, the fraction is p divided by d when base is 1, otherwise base to the power p minus 1, divided by base to the power d minus 1. When za equals zb it skips straight to the second gap. The result is never below 0.

`rule_color(r, dark)` is the rule's dark color when dark is true, else its light color.

`label_text(layer, a, out)` appends the text a label shows to out: for the housenumber layer the house number; otherwise the latin name when it is not empty, else the name, else the English name; for the transportation_name layer, when all three are empty, the ref. For the mountain_peak layer, when ele_ft is 0 or more, a newline and the elevation with thousands separators and " ft" follow the name (so "Mount Hood", newline, "11,249 ft").

`poi_dot(cls)` is the dot color for a POI class string: 0xe07b3a for restaurant, fast_food, cafe, bar, pub, ice_cream, bakery, beer and food; 0x9b59c7 for shop, grocery, supermarket, clothing_store, convenience, mall, alcohol_shop, department_store and jewelry; 0xd9534f for hospital, pharmacy, doctors, dentist, clinic and veterinary; 0x9c7a4a for school, college, university, library, kindergarten and museum; 0x3b7dd8 for bus, railway, airport, ferry_terminal, fuel, parking, bicycle_rental, car, aerialway and harbor; 0x4a9e5c for park, playground, garden, sports, pitch, zoo, campsite, golf, swimming, stadium and attraction; 0x8a5cc7 for lodging; 0x777777 for place_of_worship; 0x8a8f99 for anything else.

`label_style(layer, gtype, a)` picks how a feature is labelled, as a LabelStyle whose ok is false when it is not labelled. Colors given as one value apply to both looks unless a dark value is named; the default color is 0x333333 with dark 0xe6e8eb, and fonts default to F_REGULAR. Rules by layer, using the class string cls_s and rank (a rank of 0 counts as 10):
- place: "continent" minz 0 maxz 2 size 14 bold pri 0; "country" bold pri 10 plus rank, size 15 when rank is 2 or less else 13, minz 1 for rank 1, 2 for rank 2, 3 otherwise, maxz 9, color 0x334455 dark 0xd8dde4; "state" and "province" pri 30 plus rank, minz 5, maxz 10, size 12, color 0x667788 dark 0xa9b2bd; "city" pri 20 plus rank (pri minus 1 when capital is 2), size 16 when rank is 3 or less else 14, minz 3 for rank 3 or less, 5 for rank up to 7, 7 for rank up to 9, else 8, maxz 15; "town" pri 40 plus rank, size 13, minz 7, maxz 17; "village" pri 50 plus rank, size 12, minz 9, maxz 18; "suburb" and "quarter" pri 60 plus rank, size 12, minz 11, maxz 18, color 0x555555 dark 0xc5cad1; "neighbourhood" pri 65, size 11, minz 13, maxz 19, color 0x666666 dark 0xb2b8c0; "hamlet", "isolated_dwelling" and "locality" pri 70, size 11, minz 12, maxz 19; "island" italic pri 55, size 12, minz 9; any other class is not labelled.
- water_name: italic with color 0x495e91 dark 0x8fb4d8; "ocean" pri 5 size 14 minz 0 maxz 8; "sea", "bay" and "strait" pri 35 size 12 minz 3 maxz 14; anything else pri 45 size 12 minz 9.
- transportation_name: line true, color 0x555555 dark 0xc8ccd2; "motorway" and "trunk" pri 100 size 12 minz 13; "primary" pri 101 size 12 minz 13; "secondary" and "tertiary" pri 103 size 12 minz 13; "minor" and "service" pri 110 size 11 minz 15; "path" and "track" pri 120 size 11 minz 16; anything else is not labelled.
- poi: pri 200 plus rank, size 11, color 0x666666 dark 0xb8bcc4, dot `poi_dot(cls_s)`, minz 15 when rank is 7 or less, 16 when it is 20 or less, else 17.
- housenumber: pri 400, size 10, minz 17, color 0x888888 dark 0x9aa0a8.
- mountain_peak: pri 150 plus rank, size 11, minz 12, color 0x725a3a dark 0xc9b08a, dot 0x8a6a44.
- aerodrome_label: pri 140, size 11, minz 10, color 0x555555 dark 0xc5cad1, dot 0x3b7dd8.
- every other layer is not labelled.
